 at the center, and no polls, ratings, or market prices justify moving far from that. Heavy coverage of Tom Tiffany's efforts to overturn the 2020 election and Democrats avoiding a socialist nominee give a marginal edge to the Democratic ticket, but not enough to break the tossup band.", "watch": "Any actual Wisconsin polling, plus whether the 2020-certification controversy moves swing voters in the Milwaukee and Fox Valley suburbs.", "confidence": "low", "notes": ["No expert ratings published yet; forecast rests on fundamentals and polls.", "New or vacant seat with no expert ratings; fundamentals only.", "No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings."]}, "overview": "Wisconsin remains one of the narrowest battlegrounds in the country, and the 2028 race opens with no incumbent on the ballot and essentially no polling to guide expectations. The state's even partisan lean makes either ticket's win plausible, and the forecast sits almost exactly at even.\n\nThe campaign has been shaped by Republican Tom Tiffany's defense of his 2020 election-overturn efforts, a controversy that dominates recent coverage even as he pledges to certify the 2028 results. Democrats dodged a risk by defeating a democratic socialist in their gubernatorial primary, suggesting a moderate-leaning ticket. With thin evidence, uncertainty is wide and small shifts could tip the state either way.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.498, "margin": 0.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.4982, "margin": 0.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.5145, "margin": 0.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.4971, "margin": 0.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.5003, "margin": 0.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.498, "margin": 0.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.5067, "margin": 0.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.5039, "margin": 0.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.5006, "margin": 0.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.4971, "margin": 0.0}, {"da